{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/claude-code/evals/quiet-explore/graders/no-record.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-09-29T14:06:38.814963Z","id":"acda5d4130652ca7db314189b2154c291d27812f35200108ec78e9efd3269a32","body":{"detail":"quiet-explore, quiet-question, and quiet-typo (plugins/claude-code/evals/quiet-explore/graders/no-record.md, plugins/claude-code/evals/quiet-question/graders/no-record.md, plugins/claude-code/evals/quiet-typo/graders/no-record.md -- identical grader in all three) assert silence only via a tool_used grader on Bash, matching qualifier/ensure-qualifier.sh invocations of record|reply|resolve|emit. All three cases' prompt.md list allowed_tools: [Read, Glob, Grep, Edit, Write, Bash, Skill], and plugins/claude-code/README.md's documented invocation additionally grants --allow-tools Write Edit Bash, so Write and Edit are actually available in the run. A run that appended a metabox JSONL line straight to an existing .qual file via the Write or Edit tool, bypassing the qualifier binary entirely, would leave no matching Bash call, so this grader would still pass even though a record was in effect written.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":7},"content_hash":"fa84221728cb89292caec56d2e80ab2d4744356d7b3b5873bd73018ab3ac1804"},"suggested_fix":"Add a second grader (or extend this one) that also flags Write/Edit calls touching a *.qual path, e.g. a tool_used grader on Write and Edit with input_match matching '\\.qual' and min:0/max:0, or grade the fixture's .qual file contents against their pre-run state.","summary":"no-record graders only watch Bash for the qualifier CLI pattern, not Write/Edit calls that could append straight to a .qual file","tags":["review","review:claude-plugin-pr14","session:claude-code:6982e520-2dd9-4d9d-b484-c954e628c65c"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/claude-code/evals/quiet-explore/graders/no-record.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-09-29T14:17:14.839105Z","id":"e7f4b6eadaf4d679c440244ec80e6813a131349fba4396a38f7662648087fe29","body":{"detail":"plugins/claude-code/evals/quiet-{explore,question,typo}/graders/no-record.md are byte-identical (same md5) and each is the only grader in its case. Each is 'tool: Bash' with input_match on qualifier / ensure-qualifier.sh exec followed by record|reply|resolve|emit (line 4). All three prompt.md files have 'allowed_tools: [Read, Glob, Grep, Edit, Write, Bash, Skill]' (line 3), and plugins/claude-code/README.md:73,76 run the suite with '--allow-tools Write Edit Bash'. A Write or Edit call that appends to a .qual file therefore matches no grader. The plugin-evals docs (https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugin-evals.md, grader table) describe a '{ source: file, path: <path> }' input that could grade the .qual file contents after the run.","kind":"comment","references":"acda5d4130652ca7db314189b2154c291d27812f35200108ec78e9efd3269a32","summary":"confirmed: the no-record graders only watch Bash, while Write and Edit are also granted","tags":["verified","session:claude-code:6982e520-2dd9-4d9d-b484-c954e628c65c"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/claude-code/evals/quiet-explore/graders/no-record.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T17:00:14.409263Z","id":"f1b4cfc074ee78d0af46106e5713c1b07717d4707be92046e71788cc46733567","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:6a733e989f42ba0d270a61225768f5959841d00f","summary":"no-write-qual.md and no-edit-qual.md now sit beside no-record.md, matching Write/Edit calls whose file_path ends .qual, so a direct write or edit to a .qual file is caught where the Bash-only grader could not see it: scripts/test-plugin.sh ok: eval graders: no-skill-fired matches every qual skill; no-record cases also forbid .qual writes; the Bash-side matcher was also hardened by commits e29f44452e62ee09f4abbd9d82ab228cf2e07878 and c98badb917a3023cbd4153b162b4c2e6bb3ad1a1, verified by ok: eval graders: Bash graders match only the command, and name qualifier --help's subcommands","supersedes":"acda5d4130652ca7db314189b2154c291d27812f35200108ec78e9efd3269a32","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6982e520-2dd9-4d9d-b484-c954e628c65c"]}}
